      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we first need to determine the number of terms in the arithmetic sequence and then find the sum of the sequence. Finally, we will find the remainder of this sum when divided by 6.\n\nThe given sequence is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). The general term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[a_n = a + (n-1)d\\]\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in the sequence. The last term \\(a_n = 259\\). So, we solve for \\(n\\):\n\\[259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\\]\n\\[259 = 1 + 6n - 6\\]\n\\[259 = 6n - 5\\]\n\\[264 = 6n\\]\n\\[n = 44\\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Here, \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(l = 259\\). So, the sum is:\n\\[S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We can do this by finding the remainder of 5720 divided by 6:\n\\[5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is:\n\\[\\boxed{2}\\]",
