      "text": "The given sum is an arithmetic series with the first term $a = 1$, common difference $d = 6$, and last term $l = 259$.\nThe number of terms in the series can be found by using the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic series, which is $a_n = a + (n-1)d$.\nSetting $a_n = 259$, we have $259 = 1 + (n-1)6$, which gives $n = 44$.\nThe sum of an arithmetic series can be found using the formula $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a+l)$, so the sum of the series is $S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2}(1+259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720$.\nTo find the remainder when $5720$ is divided by $6$, we can find the remainder of each term when divided by $6$ and add them up.\nThe remainders of the terms when divided by $6$ are $1, 7, 13, 19, \\dots, 253, 259$.\nThe remainders form an arithmetic series with the first term $1$, common difference $6$, and last term $1$.\nThere are $44$ terms in this series, so the sum of the remainders is $44(1+1)/2 = 44$.\nTherefore, the remainder when $5720$ is divided by $6$ is $44 \\div 6 = \\boxed{2}$.The answer is: 2",
