      "text": "To determine the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we first need to identify the number of terms in the sequence and then find the sum of the sequence.\n\nThe given sequence is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). The general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[a_n = a + (n-1)d\\]\nSetting \\(a_n = 259\\), we can solve for \\(n\\):\n\\[259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\\]\n\\[259 = 1 + 6n - 6\\]\n\\[259 = 6n - 5\\]\n\\[264 = 6n\\]\n\\[n = 44\\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nNext, we find the sum of the arithmetic sequence. The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Here, \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(l = 259\\). Substituting these values in, we get:\n\\[S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by dividing 5720 by 6:\n\\[5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is:\n\\[\\boxed{2}\\]",
